{"uid":"18501c0ef57d128d","name":"test_a_cured_when_refused_by_the_bounded_lint_stays_a_criterion_bound_violation","fullName":"tests.test_cured_when#test_a_cured_when_refused_by_the_bounded_lint_stays_a_criterion_bound_violation","historyId":"3c84247c6f2a496f549b64816ed7efad","time":{"start":1791881088610,"stop":1791881088615,"duration":5},"description":"`cured_when` is checked by the SAME bounded-checkable-clause lint a\n    planner's own `successCriteria` is (`plan_ingestion.lint_proposal`) --\n    an oversized `cured_when` is refused by `review_cured_when_errors`\n    with the identical message shape `lint_proposal` itself uses for an\n    oversized task criterion (the '~N-clause bound' phrase), not a\n    second, differently-worded rule.\n\n    #209 defect 1: the IDENTICAL bound still applies, and this node still\n    proves it is the same rule with the same wording -- what changed is\n    which overruns reach the refusal. An overrun with a lossless,\n    lint-clean fold is REPAIRED at `state.insert_cure_tasks`\n    (`plan_ingestion.repair_criteria`) instead of refused, because the\n    refusal spent a review contract attempt re-asking a hat for advice the\n    harness had already computed and then, since `_step_review` discards\n    those contract errors, used the refused text verbatim anyway. Only an\n    UN-repairable overrun is still a criterion-bound violation, so this\n    node's fixture moved from the repairable seven-clause string to one\n    whose sixth clause is itself unsatisfiable; the assertion it makes is\n    unchanged.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p><code>cured_when</code> is checked by the SAME bounded-checkable-clause lint a<br />\nplanner's own <code>successCriteria</code> is (<code>plan_ingestion.lint_proposal</code>) --<br />\nan oversized <code>cured_when</code> is refused by <code>review_cured_when_errors</code><br />\nwith the identical message shape <code>lint_proposal</code> itself uses for an<br />\noversized task criterion (the '~N-clause bound' phrase), not a<br />\nsecond, differently-worded rule.</p>\n<pre><code>#209 defect 1: the IDENTICAL bound still applies, and this node still\nproves it is the same rule with the same wording -- what changed is\nwhich overruns reach the refusal. An overrun with a lossless,\nlint-clean fold is REPAIRED at `state.insert_cure_tasks`\n(`plan_ingestion.repair_criteria`) instead of refused, because the\nrefusal spent a review contract attempt re-asking a hat for advice the\nharness had already computed and then, since `_step_review` discards\nthose contract errors, used the refused text verbatim anyway. Only an\nUN-repairable overrun is still a criterion-bound violation, so this\nnode's fixture moved from the repairable seven-clause string to one\nwhose sixth clause is itself unsatisfiable; the assertion it makes is\nunchanged.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791880795115,"stop":1791880795116,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791880795116,"stop":1791880795116,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791881088584,"stop":1791881088595,"duration":11},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791881088584,"stop":1791881088584,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCoun